// Auto-generated for the Unit Board — TOEIC Themed Vocabulary
window.TC_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"Accident 意外事故","cards":[{"w":"collision","p":"n.","d":"a crash in which two things hit each other","c":"碰撞；相撞","s":"A: Why are all the delivery trucks late this morning? B: There was a collision between two buses on the highway, so traffic is blocked for miles.","t":"A：為什麼今天早上所有的送貨卡車都遲到了？ B：高速公路上兩輛公車發生了【碰撞】，所以車流堵塞了好幾英里。"},{"w":"crash","p":"n.","d":"an accident in which a vehicle hits something hard","c":"撞車；車禍；墜毀","s":"A: Did the sales manager make it to the conference in Chicago? B: No, he missed it because a car crash closed the main road to the airport, and he had to take a longer route.","t":"A：業務經理有趕上芝加哥的研討會嗎？ B：沒有，他錯過了，因為一場【車禍】封閉了通往機場的主要道路，他只好繞遠路。"},{"w":"incident","p":"n.","d":"something unusual or bad that happens","c":"事件；事故","s":"A: Should I tell the supervisor that a box fell from the shelf in the warehouse? B: Yes, every incident must be recorded in the safety log, even if no one was injured.","t":"A：倉庫裡有個箱子從架子上掉下來，我應該告訴主管嗎？ B：要，每一起【事件】都必須記錄在安全日誌裡，即使沒有人受傷。"},{"w":"mishap","p":"n.","d":"a small accident or piece of bad luck","c":"小意外；小差錯","s":"A: How did the product launch go yesterday? B: It went well overall, but there was a small mishap when the projector stopped working, so we had to present without slides.","t":"A：昨天的產品發表會進行得如何？ B：整體很順利，但投影機故障時出了個小【意外】，所以我們只好在沒有投影片的情況下報告。"},{"w":"injury","p":"n.","d":"harm done to a person's body","c":"傷害；受傷","s":"A: Why is Tom working from home this week? B: He got a back injury while he was lifting heavy boxes in the storeroom, and his doctor told him to rest for a few days.","t":"A：湯姆這週為什麼在家工作？ B：他在儲藏室搬重箱子時背部【受傷】了，醫生要他休息幾天。"},{"w":"damage","p":"n.","d":"harm done to a thing so it is broken or worth less","c":"損壞；損害","s":"A: Has the insurance company checked the delivery van yet? B: Yes, they came this morning, and they said the damage to the front door will cost about two thousand dollars to repair.","t":"A：保險公司檢查過那輛送貨車了嗎？ B：檢查過了，他們今天早上來過，說前門的【損壞】大約要花兩千元修理。"},{"w":"wound","p":"n.","d":"a cut or hurt place on the body","c":"傷口","s":"A: The new worker cut his hand on a sharp metal sheet at the factory. B: The nurse cleaned the wound and covered it with a bandage, and then she told him to wear gloves next time.","t":"A：新來的員工在工廠被一片鋒利的金屬板割傷了手。 B：護士清潔了【傷口】並用繃帶包紮，然後叮嚀他下次要戴手套。"},{"w":"emergency","p":"n.","d":"a sudden, dangerous situation that needs fast action","c":"緊急情況","s":"A: What should we do if the fire alarm rings during the meeting? B: In an emergency, please leave the building by the nearest stairway, and don't use the elevators.","t":"A：如果開會時火災警報響了，我們該怎麼做？ B：遇到【緊急情況】時，請從最近的樓梯離開大樓，不要搭電梯。"},{"w":"ambulance","p":"n.","d":"a vehicle that takes sick or hurt people to hospital","c":"救護車","s":"A: One of the visitors fainted in the lobby, and she isn't waking up. B: Call an ambulance right away, and ask the security guard to keep the area clear until help arrives.","t":"A：有一位訪客在大廳昏倒了，一直沒有醒來。 B：馬上叫【救護車】，並請警衛在救援到達前淨空該區域。"},{"w":"rescue","p":"v.","d":"to save someone from danger","c":"救援；營救","s":"A: Was anyone trapped when the old storage building caught fire last night? B: Two workers were inside, but the firefighters managed to rescue them before the roof fell down.","t":"A：昨晚舊倉庫失火時，有人被困住嗎？ B：有兩名員工在裡面，但消防員在屋頂塌下來之前成功把他們【救出】。"},{"w":"survive","p":"v.","d":"to stay alive or keep going after something bad","c":"倖存；存活；撐過","s":"A: I heard about the plane that made an emergency landing near the coast. B: Yes, it was frightening, but all the passengers managed to survive, and only a few of them needed hospital care.","t":"A：我聽說有架飛機在海岸附近緊急降落。 B：對，真的很嚇人，但所有乘客都【倖存】了，只有少數幾人需要住院治療。"},{"w":"collapse","p":"v.","d":"to fall down suddenly","c":"倒塌；崩塌","s":"A: Why is the parking garage closed to all employees today? B: Engineers are worried that part of the second floor could collapse after the heavy rain, so they are checking the structure.","t":"A：為什麼今天停車場不開放給所有員工？ B：工程師擔心大雨過後二樓有一部分可能會【倒塌】，所以他們正在檢查結構。"},{"w":"slip","p":"v.","d":"to slide by accident and lose your balance","c":"滑倒；滑跤","s":"A: Why is there a yellow sign in front of the restroom? B: The cleaner just mopped the floor, and the sign warns people that they might slip if they walk too quickly.","t":"A：洗手間前面為什麼放了一個黃色標誌？ B：清潔人員剛拖完地，這個標誌是提醒大家走太快可能會【滑倒】。"},{"w":"fall","p":"v.","d":"to drop down to the ground by accident","c":"跌落；掉落；跌倒","s":"A: Why do we need to wear hard hats on the construction site? B: Tools sometimes fall from the higher floors, and a helmet can protect your head from serious harm.","t":"A：為什麼我們在工地必須戴安全帽？ B：工具有時會從較高的樓層【掉落】，而安全帽可以保護你的頭部免受嚴重傷害。"},{"w":"trip","p":"v.","d":"to hit your foot on something and almost fall","c":"絆倒；絆到","s":"A: Can you move these cables away from the walkway in the office? B: Sure, someone could trip over them and get hurt, and the safety inspector is coming this afternoon.","t":"A：你能把這些電線從辦公室走道移開嗎？ B：當然，可能會有人被它們【絆倒】而受傷，而且安全檢查員今天下午就要來了。"},{"w":"careless","p":"adj.","d":"not paying enough attention; not careful","c":"粗心的；不小心的","s":"A: How did the forklift hit the shelf in the warehouse? B: The driver was careless and looked at his phone while he was driving, so the manager gave him a written warning.","t":"A：堆高機怎麼會撞上倉庫的貨架？ B：司機很【粗心】，開車時一直看手機，所以經理給了他書面警告。"},{"w":"dangerous","p":"adj.","d":"likely to hurt someone or cause harm","c":"危險的","s":"A: Is it okay to store these chemicals next to the heater? B: No, that is very dangerous because they can catch fire easily, so please move them to the cool storage room.","t":"A：可以把這些化學藥品放在暖氣旁邊嗎？ B：不行，那非常【危險】，因為它們很容易起火，所以請把它們移到陰涼的儲藏室。"},{"w":"serious","p":"adj.","d":"very bad and worrying","c":"嚴重的","s":"A: Was the accident at the factory last week serious? B: Fortunately not, because the two workers only had small cuts, but the machine was badly damaged and needs to be replaced.","t":"A：上週工廠的事故【嚴重】嗎？ B：幸好不嚴重，兩名員工只受了小割傷，但機器嚴重損壞，需要更換。"},{"w":"minor","p":"adj.","d":"small and not very serious","c":"輕微的；次要的","s":"A: Do we need to cancel the company trip because of the bus accident? B: No, it was only a minor accident, and the bus company is sending another vehicle, so we can still leave on time.","t":"A：因為遊覽車的事故，我們需要取消員工旅遊嗎？ B：不用，那只是個【輕微的】事故，而且客運公司會另派一輛車，所以我們還是可以準時出發。"},{"w":"unexpected","p":"adj.","d":"not expected; surprising","c":"意外的；出乎意料的","s":"A: Why did the shipment from Japan arrive three days late? B: There was an unexpected storm along the coast, and the ship had to wait in the port until the weather improved.","t":"A：從日本來的貨為什麼晚了三天才到？ B：沿海出現了一場【出乎意料的】暴風雨，船只好在港口等到天氣好轉。"},{"w":"suddenly","p":"adv.","d":"quickly and without any warning","c":"突然地","s":"A: What happened during the presentation this morning? B: The lights suddenly went out in the whole building, and we had to finish the meeting in the dark.","t":"A：今天早上的簡報發生了什麼事？ B：整棟大樓的燈【突然】熄滅了，我們只好在黑暗中把會議開完。"},{"w":"fortunately","p":"adv.","d":"luckily; used before good news","c":"幸運地；幸好","s":"A: I heard that a delivery truck hit the front gate of our office this morning. B: Yes, it did, but fortunately, nobody was standing near the gate, and the driver was not hurt either.","t":"A：我聽說今天早上有輛送貨卡車撞上了我們辦公室的大門。 B：對，是有這件事，但【幸好】當時沒有人站在大門附近，司機也沒有受傷。"},{"w":"unfortunately","p":"adv.","d":"sadly; used before bad news","c":"不幸地；遺憾地","s":"A: Will Ms. Lin be able to give her speech at the conference tomorrow? B: unfortunately, she hurt her ankle while she was jogging, so her assistant will speak in her place.","t":"A：林小姐明天能在研討會上演講嗎？ B：【很遺憾】，她慢跑時扭傷了腳踝，所以會由她的助理代替她發言。"},{"w":"carefully","p":"adv.","d":"with close attention so you don't make mistakes or get hurt","c":"小心地；仔細地","s":"A: Is there anything I should know before I use the new cutting machine? B: Read the instructions carefully and always wear safety glasses, because small pieces of metal can fly out.","t":"A：在使用新的切割機之前，有什麼我該知道的嗎？ B：要【仔細地】閱讀說明書，並且一定要戴護目鏡，因為小金屬碎片可能會飛出來。"},{"w":"witness","p":"n.","d":"a person who sees something happen","c":"目擊者；證人","s":"A: Did anyone see the car hit the bicycle outside our store? B: Yes, one of our cashiers was a witness, and she has already told the police exactly what she saw.","t":"A：有人看到那輛車在我們店外撞上腳踏車嗎？ B：有，我們的一位收銀員是【目擊者】，她已經把看到的情況詳細告訴警方了。"},{"w":"report","p":"v.","d":"to tell a person in charge about something that happened","c":"報告；通報","s":"A: What should I do if I see broken equipment in the lab? B: You should report it to the safety officer immediately, and you should put a \"Do Not Use\" sign on it.","t":"A：如果我在實驗室看到損壞的設備，我該怎麼做？ B：你應該立刻向安全負責人【通報】，並且在設備上貼上「請勿使用」的標示。"},{"w":"investigate","p":"v.","d":"to try to find out the facts about something","c":"調查","s":"A: Does anyone know why the machine on Line 3 caught fire? B: Not yet, but the safety team will investigate the problem this week, and they will share their findings with all staff.","t":"A：有人知道三號生產線的機器為什麼起火嗎？ B：還不知道，但安全小組本週會【調查】這個問題，並將調查結果告知全體員工。"},{"w":"cause","p":"n.","d":"the reason why something happens","c":"原因；起因","s":"A: Have the engineers found out why the elevator stopped between floors? B: Yes, they said the cause was an electrical problem, and the elevator will be fixed by Friday.","t":"A：工程師查出電梯為什麼卡在樓層之間了嗎？ B：查出來了，他們說【原因】是電力問題，電梯會在星期五前修好。"},{"w":"prevent","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from happening","c":"預防；防止","s":"A: Why are we putting new rubber mats at the entrance? B: The mats will help prevent accidents on rainy days, because the floor near the door gets very wet.","t":"A：我們為什麼要在入口放新的橡膠地墊？ B：這些地墊有助於【預防】雨天發生意外，因為門口附近的地板會變得很濕。"},{"w":"safety","p":"n.","d":"the state of being safe from danger or harm","c":"安全","s":"A: Do new employees have to attend any training before they start? B: Yes, everyone must attend a safety workshop on the first day, and they learn how to use the fire extinguishers.","t":"A：新進員工開始工作前必須參加任何訓練嗎？ B：要，每個人第一天都必須參加【安全】研習，學習如何使用滅火器。"},{"w":"recover","p":"v.","d":"to get well again after being sick or hurt","c":"康復；恢復","s":"A: When will Mr. Chen come back to the office after his car accident? B: His doctor says he needs about two weeks to recover, so we will share his projects until he returns.","t":"A：陳先生出車禍後什麼時候會回辦公室？ B：他的醫生說他大約需要兩週時間【康復】，所以在他回來之前我們會分擔他的專案。"},{"w":"shock","p":"n.","d":"a sudden, strong feeling of surprise or fear after something bad","c":"震驚；驚嚇","s":"A: How is the driver who was in the accident on Main Street? B: He was not badly hurt, but he was in shock for a while, so the paramedics kept him in the ambulance.","t":"A：在緬因街出車禍的那位駕駛還好嗎？ B：他沒有受重傷，但有一段時間處於【驚嚇】狀態，所以急救人員讓他待在救護車上。"},{"w":"treatment","p":"n.","d":"medical care for an illness or injury","c":"治療","s":"A: Does our company insurance pay for hospital costs after a work accident? B: Yes, it covers all medical treatment for injuries at work, but you must submit the forms within thirty days.","t":"A：公司的保險會支付工作意外後的醫療費用嗎？ B：會，它涵蓋所有工作傷害的醫療【治療】費用，但你必須在三十天內遞交表格。"},{"w":"traffic","p":"n.","d":"the cars and other vehicles on a road","c":"交通；車流","s":"A: Should we leave now for the airport to meet the clients? B: Yes, there was an accident on the bridge, so the traffic will be heavy, and we don't want to be late.","t":"A：我們現在該出發去機場接客戶了嗎？ B：對，橋上發生了事故，所以【交通】會很擁擠，我們可不想遲到。"}]}];
